1
00:00:03,592 --> 00:00:05,794
[SPEAKER_04]: You were born here in, is it Napa or Napa?

2
00:00:05,954 --> 00:00:06,234
[SPEAKER_04]: Napa.

3
00:00:06,274 --> 00:00:06,614
[SPEAKER_04]: Napa?

4
00:00:06,795 --> 00:00:07,115
[SPEAKER_04]: Napa.

5
00:00:07,615 --> 00:00:10,117
[SPEAKER_04]: In January 16th, 1894?

6
00:00:10,157 --> 00:00:10,617
[SPEAKER_04]: Ninety-five.

7
00:00:10,997 --> 00:00:11,598
[SPEAKER_03]: Ninety-five.

8
00:00:11,738 --> 00:00:12,358
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah.

9
00:00:12,418 --> 00:00:14,280
[SPEAKER_03]: The record book says ninety-four, huh?

10
00:00:14,940 --> 00:00:16,561
[SPEAKER_03]: How old are you?

11
00:00:17,382 --> 00:00:18,783
[SPEAKER_04]: Eighty-three, right?

12
00:00:18,803 --> 00:00:19,483
[SPEAKER_04]: Eighty-three, yeah.

13
00:00:19,523 --> 00:00:23,146
[SPEAKER_04]: Eighty-three last January.

14
00:00:23,166 --> 00:00:24,567
[SPEAKER_04]: Did your family always live here?

15
00:00:24,587 --> 00:00:25,187
[SPEAKER_04]: Oh, yes.

16
00:00:25,507 --> 00:00:26,628
[SPEAKER_04]: Yes, they always lived here.

17
00:00:28,129 --> 00:00:29,430
[SPEAKER_04]: And did your father play ball?

18
00:00:29,550 --> 00:00:30,030
[SPEAKER_04]: No.

19
00:00:30,911 --> 00:00:31,651
[SPEAKER_04]: He was a farmer.

20
00:00:32,112 --> 00:00:32,472
[SPEAKER_04]: I see.

21
00:00:36,079 --> 00:00:38,521
[SPEAKER_04]: Where did his father come from?

22
00:00:38,641 --> 00:00:39,482
[SPEAKER_04]: Someplace else?

23
00:00:39,582 --> 00:00:39,822
[SPEAKER_04]: Italy.

24
00:00:39,882 --> 00:00:40,703
[SPEAKER_04]: He came from Italy.

25
00:00:40,783 --> 00:00:41,264
[SPEAKER_04]: Oh, he was?

26
00:00:41,364 --> 00:00:42,445
[SPEAKER_03]: Oh, I see.

27
00:00:42,465 --> 00:00:43,946
[SPEAKER_04]: How'd he happen to settle out here, I wonder?

28
00:00:44,847 --> 00:00:49,391
[SPEAKER_03]: Well, this is a wine country, you know, and there's a lot of Italians settled here from Italy.

29
00:00:49,751 --> 00:00:51,813
[SPEAKER_03]: Lots of them.

30
00:00:51,893 --> 00:00:58,439
[SPEAKER_03]: And you find, if you look through the phone book, you see a lot of Italian names, fourth and fifth generation, now.

31
00:00:58,799 --> 00:00:59,040
[SPEAKER_03]: I see.

32
00:01:00,957 --> 00:01:02,858
[SPEAKER_03]: And that's the kind we used to have at home.

33
00:01:04,259 --> 00:01:11,284
[SPEAKER_03]: At least I can think of five hotels that were run by Italians, four Italian people.

34
00:01:11,845 --> 00:01:14,346
[SPEAKER_03]: They worked on the vineyards and the fruits and the tanneries.

35
00:01:16,688 --> 00:01:18,229
[SPEAKER_03]: Where'd you first play ball?

36
00:01:18,369 --> 00:01:20,050
[SPEAKER_03]: You had a sandlot ball around here?

37
00:01:20,410 --> 00:01:21,151
[SPEAKER_03]: Oh yeah, right here.

38
00:01:21,171 --> 00:01:26,855
[SPEAKER_03]: We had a little team called the Alta Heights.

39
00:01:28,573 --> 00:01:30,594
[SPEAKER_03]: We used to play with St. Louis.

40
00:01:31,755 --> 00:01:34,137
[SPEAKER_03]: Our main opponent was St. Helena.

41
00:01:35,398 --> 00:01:37,519
[SPEAKER_03]: And Dutch Juni was one of the St. Louis.

42
00:01:37,559 --> 00:01:40,841
[SPEAKER_03]: He was also a ballplayer professional afterwards.

43
00:01:40,861 --> 00:01:42,062
[SPEAKER_03]: Juni.

44
00:01:42,082 --> 00:01:42,802
[SPEAKER_03]: J-U-N-I-Y.

45
00:01:42,822 --> 00:01:43,703
[SPEAKER_03]: He's dead now.

46
00:01:43,723 --> 00:01:47,005
[SPEAKER_03]: He's been gone quite a little while.

47
00:01:47,045 --> 00:01:52,489
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, this was around 1906 and 7 and 8.

48
00:01:52,509 --> 00:01:53,930
[SPEAKER_03]: We were kids.

49
00:01:53,950 --> 00:01:55,351
[SPEAKER_04]: What position did you play in those days?

50
00:01:55,371 --> 00:01:55,871
[SPEAKER_03]: First base.

51
00:01:55,951 --> 00:01:56,792
[SPEAKER_03]: Always first base.

52
00:01:58,377 --> 00:02:00,358
[SPEAKER_04]: Did you have a high school here in Napa you went to?

53
00:02:00,418 --> 00:02:00,698
[SPEAKER_04]: Oh yeah.

54
00:02:00,818 --> 00:02:01,979
[SPEAKER_04]: Did you play on the team there?

55
00:02:01,999 --> 00:02:02,619
[SPEAKER_03]: Did you have a team?

56
00:02:02,639 --> 00:02:02,739
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

57
00:02:02,759 --> 00:02:04,260
[SPEAKER_03]: Caught without a mask one day.

58
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:05,761
[SPEAKER_03]: That finished me in for catching.

59
00:02:05,821 --> 00:02:05,921
[SPEAKER_03]: Oh?

60
00:02:06,241 --> 00:02:06,761
[SPEAKER_03]: What happened?

61
00:02:06,781 --> 00:02:07,541
[SPEAKER_03]: It hit me in the eye.

62
00:02:07,561 --> 00:02:08,922
[SPEAKER_03]: Why didn't you have a mask on?

63
00:02:08,942 --> 00:02:10,003
[SPEAKER_03]: We didn't have any masks.

64
00:02:10,083 --> 00:02:10,743
[SPEAKER_03]: Is that right?

65
00:02:10,763 --> 00:02:12,044
[SPEAKER_03]: We didn't have any.

66
00:02:13,284 --> 00:02:14,405
[SPEAKER_03]: Or at least they forgot it.

67
00:02:14,485 --> 00:02:15,005
[SPEAKER_03]: I don't know.

68
00:02:15,805 --> 00:02:18,006
[SPEAKER_04]: And you went out of St. Mary's, right?

69
00:02:18,026 --> 00:02:18,667
[SPEAKER_03]: St. Mary's, yeah.

70
00:02:18,747 --> 00:02:20,568
[SPEAKER_03]: What did you plan to do at St. Mary's?

71
00:02:20,608 --> 00:02:21,688
[SPEAKER_03]: What was your major field?

72
00:02:21,708 --> 00:02:22,669
[SPEAKER_03]: Did you have anything in particular?

73
00:02:22,689 --> 00:02:24,930
[SPEAKER_03]: Well, I was in the banking at St. Mary's.

74
00:02:25,030 --> 00:02:27,331
[SPEAKER_03]: I had a course there, a banking course.

75
00:02:28,375 --> 00:02:30,176
[SPEAKER_03]: I took that and then I went into baseball.

76
00:02:30,257 --> 00:02:33,119
[SPEAKER_04]: You had a pretty good team there, didn't you?

77
00:02:33,139 --> 00:02:33,559
[SPEAKER_03]: Same night?

78
00:02:33,579 --> 00:02:34,520
[SPEAKER_03]: Same night, yeah.

79
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:35,641
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, we had a pretty good team.

80
00:02:36,441 --> 00:02:38,843
[SPEAKER_03]: We used to play the Coastal Leagues during spring training.

81
00:02:38,983 --> 00:02:42,006
[SPEAKER_03]: Did you ever beat them?

82
00:02:42,466 --> 00:02:43,186
[SPEAKER_03]: Once in a while.

83
00:02:43,227 --> 00:02:47,970
[SPEAKER_03]: I don't think we ever did while I was playing, but the team before me did.

84
00:02:47,990 --> 00:02:52,354
[SPEAKER_03]: We had some pretty good players, like Tiny Leonard and Dutch Leonard.

85
00:02:52,374 --> 00:02:53,675
[SPEAKER_03]: Dutch Leonard, huh?

86
00:02:53,755 --> 00:02:54,035
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

87
00:02:55,563 --> 00:02:58,204
[SPEAKER_03]: In fact, they beat the Red Sox at 2-1.

88
00:02:58,324 --> 00:03:02,464
[SPEAKER_03]: I think he beat them 2-1.

89
00:03:02,504 --> 00:03:03,865
[SPEAKER_03]: They were training out here.

90
00:03:05,085 --> 00:03:08,645
[SPEAKER_04]: Did you play ball all year round out here in the good weather, or most of the year?

91
00:03:08,665 --> 00:03:10,626
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah, most of the year we played.

92
00:03:10,726 --> 00:03:14,146
[SPEAKER_04]: I noticed in the recent draft choices, so many of them come from the West Coast.

93
00:03:14,166 --> 00:03:16,727
[SPEAKER_03]: Oh, sure.

94
00:03:16,967 --> 00:03:19,807
[SPEAKER_03]: The weather is so, you know, you can play most any day.

95
00:03:20,268 --> 00:03:22,348
[SPEAKER_04]: What year did you finish up at St. Mary's?

96
00:03:23,971 --> 00:03:25,632
[SPEAKER_04]: Oh, that was... Fifteen or so?

97
00:03:25,652 --> 00:03:27,493
[SPEAKER_03]: What do you mean?

98
00:03:27,973 --> 00:03:28,494
[SPEAKER_03]: Sixteen.

99
00:03:28,654 --> 00:03:29,935
[SPEAKER_03]: Sixteen, right.

100
00:03:30,135 --> 00:03:30,595
[SPEAKER_03]: Sixteen.

101
00:03:31,435 --> 00:03:32,856
[SPEAKER_03]: And who signed you for Cleveland?

102
00:03:34,157 --> 00:03:35,638
[SPEAKER_03]: Two of the students at St. Mary's.

103
00:03:36,058 --> 00:03:37,699
[SPEAKER_03]: Not for Cleveland, but for Portland.

104
00:03:37,719 --> 00:03:39,280
[SPEAKER_03]: That's why I started with Portland.

105
00:03:40,160 --> 00:03:44,983
[SPEAKER_03]: Cleveland, Mr. Bernard, he was the vice president of Cleveland when I met him.

106
00:03:45,083 --> 00:03:45,784
[SPEAKER_04]: I see.

107
00:03:47,705 --> 00:03:48,765
[SPEAKER_03]: You mean to see you?

108
00:03:49,426 --> 00:03:51,667
[SPEAKER_03]: No, to see the manager of the Portland Club.

109
00:03:52,395 --> 00:03:53,756
[SPEAKER_03]: I didn't know anything about it, you know.

110
00:03:53,776 --> 00:03:55,357
[SPEAKER_04]: Was this McCready running Portland then?

111
00:03:55,377 --> 00:03:56,999
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, Walter McCready.

112
00:03:57,959 --> 00:04:00,221
[SPEAKER_03]: His uncle, I think, was the president.

113
00:04:02,823 --> 00:04:05,065
[SPEAKER_03]: So the St. Mary's students recommended you?

114
00:04:05,105 --> 00:04:06,126
[SPEAKER_03]: Two of them.

115
00:04:06,146 --> 00:04:06,606
[SPEAKER_03]: Both of them.

116
00:04:06,666 --> 00:04:08,487
[SPEAKER_03]: They're both alive, two of them.

117
00:04:08,607 --> 00:04:09,588
[SPEAKER_04]: Portland signed you then?

118
00:04:09,608 --> 00:04:09,969
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah.

119
00:04:10,549 --> 00:04:12,190
[SPEAKER_04]: And that was your first year in Melbourne?

120
00:04:12,210 --> 00:04:13,191
[SPEAKER_04]: That's my first year.

121
00:04:13,231 --> 00:04:13,631
[SPEAKER_04]: 1916?

122
00:04:13,851 --> 00:04:14,792
[SPEAKER_04]: 1916, yeah.

123
00:04:14,832 --> 00:04:18,235
[SPEAKER_04]: How'd you... was it a pretty big thrill going up there to the Coast League?

124
00:04:18,255 --> 00:04:18,395
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah.

125
00:04:18,415 --> 00:04:19,656
[SPEAKER_04]: Didn't think too much about it?

126
00:04:19,676 --> 00:04:20,857
[SPEAKER_03]: Never very much of it now.

127
00:04:22,362 --> 00:04:23,343
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, of course it was fun.

128
00:04:23,363 --> 00:04:31,247
[SPEAKER_03]: We were at the spring training, Sacramento, the three of us, Charlie Holliker, Carson Bigby, and myself, the three of us.

129
00:04:32,468 --> 00:04:35,830
[SPEAKER_03]: They didn't have very many, what they called, butchers in those days, you know.

130
00:04:37,131 --> 00:04:38,312
[SPEAKER_03]: Just a few of us.

131
00:04:39,032 --> 00:04:43,655
[SPEAKER_03]: And it was funny, one of the three of us went up in the big league.

132
00:04:43,675 --> 00:04:46,636
